# Toast notifications

Mutation API outcomes (create, update, delete, add, send) must use **`useToast`** from `@webonone/ui-kit` — not page-level success/warning Alerts and not hand-rolled toast DOM.

Authoritative workflow: [toast-notifications skill](../skills/toast-notifications/SKILL.md). Related: [ui-kit-consumption.mdc](ui-kit-consumption.mdc), [form-creation skill](../skills/form-creation/SKILL.md).

## Provider

Wrap the app once at the service root (`App.tsx`) with `ToastProvider`. Do **not** wrap individual pages or dialogs.

Reference: `identity/frontend/src/app/App.tsx`.

## Feedback mapping

| Feedback | Use |
|----------|-----|
| Mutation success | `toast({ title: '…' })` |
| Mutation fail | `toast({ title: '…', description?, variant: 'destructive' })` |
| Soft / non-blocking API warnings (e.g. `invite_delivery_failed`) | Do **not** show |
| Field validation | Inline `FormField` errors — [form-creation](../skills/form-creation/SKILL.md) |
| Page / list load error | `Alert` + `AlertDescription` |

## Required usage

```tsx
import { useToast } from '@webonone/ui-kit'

const { toast } = useToast()

toast({ title: 'User added' })
toast({
  title: 'Failed to add user',
  description: err instanceof Error ? err.message : undefined,
  variant: 'destructive',
})
```

## Forbidden

- Hand-rolled fixed toast markup outside `ToastProvider`
- Per-page `ToastProvider` wrappers
- Showing raw soft-warning codes (`invite_delivery_failed`, `invite_email_failed`, `invite_sms_failed`, etc.) in Alert or toast
- Using page `Alert` for mutation success or soft warnings after a successful HTTP response

